{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Seek, etc.</b> In my opinion this passage is a rebuke to the people of his generation. The meaning: after you know that you will be redeemed from Babylon and also from all the nations a second time — seek HaShem." "And the meaning of <b>in His being found</b> is to those who seek Him, for it is known that HaShem is found in every place and at every time. Rather, the meaning is before the sealing of decrees, and likewise the meaning of \"while He is near\" is an allusion to the Shekhinah, which is in the Temple."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:37.704475311Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}